# DORA Evidence Collection Scripts

A set of PowerShell scripts that connect to Microsoft Graph and Azure Resource
Manager (read-only) and gather **technical evidence** to support the DORA
Self-Assessment Tool workbook. This document explains what these scripts are,
what they are not, how to run them, and how to use what they produce.

---

## 1. What this is — and, more importantly, what it is not

**It is**: an automated way to pull real configuration data out of your Azure
and Microsoft 365 tenant — MFA policies, backup restore history, patch state,
encryption settings, and so on — and present it as structured evidence,
tagged to the same DORA Article/Section numbers used in the workbook.

**It is not**: a way to auto-complete the self-assessment. Roughly three
quarters of the questions in the DORA workbook are governance, policy, and
contractual questions (board approvals, documented procedures, vendor
contract clauses, concentration risk analysis) that no script can verify. No
API can read a contract or confirm a policy is actually followed rather than
just written down. These scripts cover the minority of questions that have
an actual technical configuration behind them — and even for those, they
report **what exists**, not **whether it's sufficient**. A human still
decides what "Yes", "Partly", or "No" means for your organization.

If you take away one thing from this document: **treat every row these
scripts produce as a prompt to investigate, not an answer to copy in.**

